# Vulnerability details

Description:

The InvestmentManager contract contains a high-severity reentrancy vulnerability in its `requestDeposit` and `requestRedeem` functions. These vulnerabilities could potentially allow an attacker to exploit the contract and manipulate the `escrow` contract's balance, leading to unexpected and malicious behavior.

**Details:**

The vulnerable functions as follows:

**In [`requestDeposit`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-centrifuge/blob/512e7a71ebd9ae76384f837204216f26380c9f91/src/InvestmentManager.sol#L117-L141) Function:**  [136](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-centrifuge/blob/512e7a71ebd9ae76384f837204216f26380c9f91/src/InvestmentManager.sol#L136)

```solidity
function requestDeposit(uint256 _currencyAmount, address user) public auth {
    // ...
    SafeTransferLib.safeTransferFrom(currency, user, address(escrow), _currencyAmount);
    // ...
}

```

**In [`requestRedeem`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-centrifuge/blob/512e7a71ebd9ae76384f837204216f26380c9f91/src/InvestmentManager.sol#L148-L172) Function:** [167](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-centrifuge/blob/512e7a71ebd9ae76384f837204216f26380c9f91/src/InvestmentManager.sol#L167)

```solidity
function requestRedeem(uint256 trancheTokenAmount, address user) public auth {
    // ...
    lPool.transferFrom(user, address(escrow), _trancheTokenAmount);
    // ...
}
```

Both functions involve external calls to other contracts (`SafeTransferLib.safeTransferFrom` in `requestDeposit` and `lPool.transferFrom` in `requestRedeem`). These external calls can be vulnerable to reentrancy attacks because the called contracts may contain arbitrary code.

