# Vulnerability details

## Impact 

The safetransferfrom function does not check the balances before and after transfers. This can lead to unlimited token minting in that an attacker can provide a custom erc20 token with a modified transferfrom function in a way that it does not transfer tokens at all while the contract thinks a real value was transferred. This is possible since centrifuge aims to support multiple currencies with the exception of tokens with more than 18 decimal places.

## Proof of Concept
   ''
  function safeTransferFrom(address token, address from, address to, uint256 value) internal {
        (bool success, bytes memory data) =
            token.call(abi.encodeWithSelector(IERC20.transferFrom.selector, from, to, value));
        require(success && (data.length == 0 || abi.decode(data, (bool))), "SafeTransferLib/safe-transfer-from-failed");
    }
    '' 
As it is this function does not check delta between the previous (before) and the current balance ( after transfer ).
