## Vulnerability Detail
The function updateTrancheTokenPrice and updatePrice lacks a timelock mechanism, which means that administrators with access can update the price of tranche tokens at any time. This opens up the possibility of price manipulation during an epoch.

## Impact
The absence of a timelock mechanism poses a centralization risk, allowing wards to manipulate tranche token prices. This manipulation can lead to malicious actions like rug-pulling, where the price of tokens is manipulated to deceive investors. Thus, causing the protocol to fail.

## Exploit Scenario
1) Ward/investors request a deposit
2) Deposit request is executed
3) Ward update the price of tokens
4) Ward call request withdraw within the epoch
5) Withdraw request is executed
6) Funds stolen

